{{!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

  Overrides `partials/header-content.hbs` from the stock Antora UI bundle
  (antora-playbook.yml pins it), which ships a demo navbar: "Products" and
  "Services" dropdowns listing Product A/B/C and Service A/B/C, every one of them
  an `href="#"`. They are placeholders for a company site that has products to
  sell, and this is one component from one repository, so they were furniture with
  dead links in it.

  The rest of the file is upstream's, unchanged, and has to stay that way: a
  supplemental file REPLACES its counterpart in the bundle rather than patching it,
  so anything dropped here is dropped from the site. That includes the search field
  above, which is inert only because SITE_SEARCH_PROVIDER is unset — delete it and
  adding search later stops working for a reason nobody will find.

  When the UI bundle updates (it is the rolling HEAD artifact), diff this against
  the new `partials/header-content.hbs` inside the zip. Nothing warns you that an
  override has gone stale.
--}}
<header class="header">
  <nav class="navbar">
    <div class="navbar-brand">
      <a class="navbar-item" href="{{{or site.url siteRootPath}}}">{{site.title}}</a>
      {{#if env.SITE_SEARCH_PROVIDER}}
      <div class="navbar-item search hide-for-print">
        <div id="search-field" class="field">
          <input id="search-input" type="text" placeholder="Search the docs"{{#if page.home}} autofocus{{/if}}>
        </div>
      </div>
      {{/if}}
      <button class="navbar-burger" aria-controls="topbar-nav" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Toggle main menu">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div id="topbar-nav" class="navbar-menu">
      <div class="navbar-end">
        <a class="navbar-item" href="#">Home</a>
        <div class="navbar-item">
          <span class="control">
            <a class="button is-primary" href="#">Download</a>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>
</header>
